    "text": "In ohm's law, we check $V=I R$ where $I$ is the corrent flowing through a resistor and $\\mathrm{V}$ is the potential difference across that resistor. Only option (a) fits the above criteria. Remember that ammeter is connected in series with resistance and voltmeter parallel with the resistance.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/n7zuUUDQEqIDoaTebgKA_rzUHZS1Tv0Hl34bIV7Jqm0.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
